WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.360
Sleep pressure is highest when you fall asleep, and it drains all night.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.180
What does a recording show?

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:14.173
Sleep is read from brain waves, eye movements and chin muscle tone.

4
00:00:15.053 --> 00:00:17.033
The night is cut into 30-second windows.

5
00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:23.493
Slower, larger brain waves mean many cortical neurons are active, then silent, in

6
00:00:23.493 --> 00:00:26.653
step. That happens as NREM sleep deepens.

7
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:32.797
In stage N3, the deepest, large slow waves take up at least a fifth of the window.

8
00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:37.087
In REM sleep, the brain waves can look much like waking.

9
00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:39.967
The eyes and the muscles tell them apart.

10
00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:43.847
So where in the night will most of the deepest sleep fall?

11
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.690
Early, when pressure is highest.

12
00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:56.310
REM sleep grows toward morning, with the clock and with time already asleep.

13
00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.710
How does the brain flip?

14
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.950
In one model, sleep-active neurons and wake-promoting groups inhibit each other.

15
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.570
Whichever side is ahead silences the other.

16
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.630
So the brain flips quickly, instead of drifting.

17
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:16.850
Once sleep wins, pressure must drain well below where sleep began before waking can

18
00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.390
win again. That memory is one way to picture the gap between the two levels.

19
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.890
Orexin neurons are thought to hold the switch on the wake side, like a finger

20
00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:28.250
holding a light switch up.

21
00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:34.190
In narcolepsy type 1, these neurons are severely reduced, and waking becomes

22
00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:38.930
unstable. Muscle tone can also fail while the person stays conscious.

23
00:01:39.983 --> 00:01:43.503
Keep this. Deep sleep mainly follows the pressure.

24
00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:46.543
REM grows with the clock and with time asleep.

25
00:01:47.443 --> 00:01:51.023
A switch with a memory may explain the gap that keeps sleep in one block.
